  "kind": "documentation-correction-and-policy-decision",
  "title": "Distinguish key shape, algebraic consistency, and full validation",
  "observed": "Ordinary EC public wrappers check prefix/coordinate widths without on-curve validation. Private consistency skips checking when either Q coordinate is absent, and width checks do not prove a scalar is in range. RSA consistency checks selected algebraic relations but not primality, distinct odd primes, or all canonical ranges; public RSA admission checks modulus storage width and absence of private fields rather than full RFC 8017 validity. RSAPublicKey.Parameters XML incorrectly describes private operations and private components. Both public parameter structs expose mutable array aliases; ECPublicKey separately caches PublicPoint so caller mutation can make representations disagree.",
